---
description: General code quality, imports, and file organization
globs: src/**/*.{ts,vue,d.ts}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Code Quality

- Follow `eslint.config.ts` for formatting and mechanical style rules.
- Remove `console.log` statements before committing.
- Remove commented-out code unless there is a documented reason to keep it.
- Clean up event listeners in `onUnmounted` hooks.
- Use meaningful names that express intent.

# File Organization

- Components live in `src/components/`.
- Composables live in `src/composables/`.
- Stores live in `src/stores/`.
- Types live in `src/types/` as `.d.ts` files.
- Utilities live in `src/utilities/`.
- Errors live in `src/errors/`.
- Views live in `src/views/` as route-level components.
- Screens live in `src/screens/` as screen-level components used in views.

# Imports

- Use `@/` for imports from `src/`.
- Use narrower aliases only when they are configured and already used in nearby
  code.
- Group imports in this order: Vue imports, third-party imports, then local
  imports.
